# Neo Tokyo Game UI

A futuristic command-based portfolio interface inspired by Japanese game UI and Swiss editorial grids.

## Key Rules

- **Left-align typography** — no centered hero layouts
- **Technical labels** above content (e.g. `SYSTEM // PORTFOLIO`)
- **Index numbers** (01, 02, 03…) for lists — monospace, muted
- **Micro labels** on the right (OPEN, VIEW, ENTER) — action-oriented
- **Grid overlays** on hero/menu — subtle white grid, ~3% opacity, 48px cells
- **Dividers** between list items, not bordered boxes
- **Colored underlines** on hover (not vertical bars) — `scaleX` 0→1, 200–300ms
- **6px horizontal shift** on row hover — precise, not soft
- **Satoshi** for display/body; monospace for technical labels
- **Sharp corners** for command UI; rounded only for primary CTAs when appropriate

## Colors

Black backgrounds, white text, zinc for secondary. Accent: cyan; rainbow motif (red/yellow/blue/pink/green) for menu items — use sparingly.
